		<name>Recall</name>
		<summary>Flashcards at natural moments, run as a trading desk for memory</summary>
		<desc>NJ's personal flashcard app. Due cards appear right after unlocking the phone
and after 15 minutes in a scrolling app; a spaced-repetition scheduler (FSRS)
decides when each card comes back. Every card is a position on a trading
desk: the book loses value while cards wait, and reviewing earns points,
ranks and awards. Cards come from NJ's Google Sheet; the app needs a setup
code to connect, so it does nothing useful for anyone else.</desc>
